519	+# CSR registration report: ax66_makatau (config 5937b880)
520	+
521	+Registered 2026-07-12 against vsim commits `e23700c` (family-aware caps) +
522	+`d0a8328` (S/U trap-CSR transport), converter commit `f62337b`
523	+(smstateen emission). Contract: `tests/engines/README.md`. Method: the
524	+three-way audit (`.claude/skills/csr-transport-bringup/references/
525	+three-way-audit.md`) -- SPEC = AndeStar_V5_SPA_UM164_V1.7 (per-CSR IM
526	+Requirement + Table 13; NOTE: UM164 is the kv-era SPA revision -- see
527	+Discrepancies); CONFIG = the build `config.inc`; RTL = the build
528	+`mk_csr_decode.v` (`andes_ip/mk_core/ucore/dru/hdl/`) `existent_csr`
529	+equation. FIRST mk_core-family registration: the CSR decoder, the config
530	+macro generation (plain-integer names, no `*_INT` twins), and several
531	+existence terms all diverge from the kv_core engines.
532	+
533	+## Engine shape (from config.inc + RTL + probe)
534	+
535	+M+S+U (`NDS_NUM_PRIVILEGE_LEVELS=3`), RV64, VLEN 128 / ELEN 64, RVH=1
536	+(hypervisor), AIA=1, SSTC=1. Perf monitor with 4 counters (Sscofpmf is a
537	+hard-1 localparam -- the Andes PMNDS scheme is hard-0 and never exists on
538	+mk), PowerBrake, PMA (16 entries), 4 debug triggers (NO tcontrol -- the
539	+decoder comments it out), 64K I$/D$ (CCTL CSRs), mstateen0-3 (ride RVH),
540	+mseccfg + mecc_code (UNCONDITIONAL in the mk decoder), no ILM/DLM (0 KB),
541	+no DSP/CoDense/StackSafe/CLIC/Smrnmi/PPI/FIO. QEMU pairing:
542	+`-cpu andes-ax66,vlen=128` -- derived at run time from the engine's
543	+`--print-qemu-config` driver globals (never the ax45mpv family default;
544	+that model silently keeps vlen=512 and models no H).
545	+
546	+## The numbers
547	+
548	+- Spec inventory rows: 232 (all in `csr_manifest.csv`)
549	+- RTL-implemented inventory addresses: 199 (probe, reset hart)
550	+- Claimed (transported) set: 35 gated names via `--describe andes_csrs`
551	+  (138 addresses including the base block, PMP mirror and PMA ranges)
552	+- `--verify` strict-compares 119 fields on this engine (rt_c_hello)
553	+
554	+## Completeness, both directions (empirical)
555	+
556	+- **Over-claims: none.** The probe cross-check (`gen_manifest.py`
557	+  recomputes it on every regeneration) reports zero claimed-but-absent
558	+  CSRs. Found and fixed during this registration: `tcontrol` (0x7A5),
559	+  `uzobctl` (0x808), `sleepvalue` (0x811) were claimed by the kv-shaped
560	+  TRIGGER/UMODE gates while the mk RTL has no existent term for any of
561	+  them.
562	+- **Under-claims: none.** Found and fixed during this registration (all
563	+  probed PRESENT while unclaimed): mseccfg, mecc_code, mpft_ctl,
564	+  mcountinhibit, mhpmcounter3-6, mhpmevent3-6, mstateen0-3, and the S/U
565	+  trio satp/medeleg/mideleg (transport decision, option A below).
566	+- Cold-cache hybrid `--verify` PASS, both trigger modes (fresh baseline
567	+  capture on this binary; the full claimed set swept on the RTL):
568	+  - marker: `[andesim] 54 cycles` / `[state-diff] PASS: 119 fields match`
569	+    / `[verify] PASS: vsim drain matches the QEMU oracle`
570	+  - pc (`--pc-start 0x100098 --pc-end 0x10009c`): identical 54-cycle
571	+    window, same PASS lines.
572	+- Generated fixtures (registration check 7): `csr_survival_gen.S`
573	+  (5 write CSRs) and `csr_readback_gen.S` (21 read-back CSRs) both
574	+  `--verify` PASS on this engine.
575	+- Caps parity: `--describe == config_inc_to_andes_caps.py` on all four
576	+  built engines (the mirror carries the same family rules).
577	+
578	+## Three-way translation table (every gated CSR)
579	+
580	+| Gate | CSRs | SPEC (UM164) | mk RTL term (mk_csr_decode.v) | binding (V<engine>_config.h) |
581	+|---|---|---|---|---|
582	+| ALWAYS | mxstatus, mclk_ctl, mnvec, mdcause | Always / Required | unconditional | -- |
583	+| POWERBRAKE | mpft_ctl | mmsc_cfg.PFT | `PFT_SUPPORT==1` (localparam 1) | `_NDS_POWERBRAKE_SUPPORT` |
584	+| ECC | mecc_code | mmsc_cfg.ECC | **unconditional** | always on mk |
585	+| EPMP | mseccfg | Optional (Smepmp/Zkr) | **unconditional** | always on mk |
586	+| PMA | pmacfg0/2, pmaaddr0-15 | mmsc_cfg.PPMA | unconditional | `_NDS_PMA_ENTRIES=16 > 0` |
587	+| PERF_MONITOR | mcountinhibit, mhpmcounter3-6, mhpmevent3-6 | Always (Zihpm) | unconditional | `_NDS_PERFORMANCE_MONITOR` |
588	+| SMSTATEEN | mstateen0-3 | Smstateen | `SMSTATEEN_SUPPORT==1` = `RVH_SUPPORT` | `_NDS_RVH_SUPPORT` |
589	+| TRIGGER | tselect, tdata1, tdata2, mcontext | Trigger Module optional | unconditional | `_NDS_NUM_TRIGGER=4 > 0` |
590	+| TCONTROL | tcontrol | Trigger Module optional | **no existent term (commented out)** | never on mk |
591	+| CCTL | mcctlbeginaddr, mcctldata | (ISZ\|DSZ) & CCTLCSR | unconditional | I$/D$ 64K > 0 |
592	+| UMODE | menvcfg, mcounteren, ucctlbeginaddr | misa[20] | unconditional | `_NDS_NUM_PRIVILEGE_LEVELS>=2` |
593	+| SMODE | mslideleg, satp, medeleg, mideleg | misa[18] | unconditional | `_NDS_NUM_PRIVILEGE_LEVELS>=3` |
594	+| PMNDS* | mcounterinten, mcounterwen, mcountermask_m/s/u | mmsc_cfg.PMNDS | **hard-0** (`PMNDS_SUPPORT=0`, `SSCOFPMF_SUPPORT=1`) | never on mk |
595	+| UZOB | uzobctl | misa.V \| mmsc_cfg3.AMM | **no existent term** | never (any family) |
596	+| ESLEEP | sleepvalue | mmsc_cfg.ESLEEP | **no existent term** | never (any family) |
597	+| DSP | ucode | mmsc_cfg.EDSP | **no existent term** | never on mk |
598	+| ALT_FP | umisc_ctl | ALT_FP_FMT \| CST_CTL | **no existent term** | never on mk |
599	+| ZCMT | jvt | Zcmt | **no existent term** | never on mk |
600	+| CODENSE | uitb | mmsc_cfg.ECD | `ISA_ECD==1` (param 0 here) | `_NDS_CODENSE_SUPPORT=0` |
601	+| STACKSAFE | mhsp_ctl, msp_bound/base | mmsc_cfg.HSP\|HSPO | `HSP_SUPPORT==1` (param 0) | `_NDS_STACKSAFE_SUPPORT=0` |
602	+| ILM/DLM | milmb/mdlmb | micm/mdcm_cfg.xLMB | `micm/mdcm` (sizes 0) | `_NDS_ILM/DLM_SIZE_KB=0` |
603	+| SMRNMI/EXCSLVL/CLIC/PPI/FIO | (their blocks) | (their conditions) | terms present, knobs off | macros absent = off |
604	+
605	+## S/U trap CSRs: transported (option A)
606	+
607	+satp/medeleg/mideleg are implemented on this S-mode core, drained by the
608	+plugin since v1, and -- new with this registration (PM decision, option
609	+A) -- restored at resume + re-read at drain + `--verify`-compared, gated
610	+on SMODE (vsim `d0a8328`; driver compare keyed on the describe names).
611	+An in-ROI read now sees the program's values instead of reset zeros.
612	+Other S-mode CSRs (sstatus, sepc, ... -- `EXCL_MODE`) remain deferred to
613	+the S/U-envelope work.
614	+
615	+## Discrepancies (classified, with evidence)
616	+
617	+1. **uzobctl 0x808 -- suspected spec-vs-RTL divergence (class D,
618	+   ESCALATE).** UM164 existence: `misa.V==1 | mmsc_cfg3.AMM==1`; this
619	+   engine has misa.V=1 (RVV configured), so the spec says EXISTS. The
620	+   probe reports ABSENT, and NEITHER decoder generation (kv_csr_dec.v,
621	+   mk_csr_decode.v) carries an existent term for 0x808. Note UM164 is the
622	+   kv-era SPA revision; the AX6x-era SPA may have moved/dropped the CSR.
623	+   Disposition: transport follows the engine (gate UZOB, off) -- but this
624	+   must be confirmed against the AX66 SPA revision and escalated to the
625	+   spec/RTL owners.
626	+2. **sleepvalue 0x811 -- interpretation-unresolved (class D-lite).**
627	+   UM164 existence: `mmsc_cfg.ESLEEP==1`. Probe: CSR absent; live
628	+   mmsc_cfg drains 0x8070e83340092015 (the ESLEEP bit position needs the
629	+   AX66-era SPA to decode with confidence). No decoder generation
630	+   implements 0x811. Same disposition and escalation as uzobctl.
631	+3. **tcontrol 0x7A5 -- none (spec-legal).** "Trigger Module optional":
632	+   the mk decoder omitting it is legal. The over-claim was OUR
633	+   translation error (class A, fixed: gate TCONTROL, vsim `e23700c`).
634	+4. **mecc_code/mseccfg unconditional -- consistent with the live
635	+   mmsc_cfg.** Present with no ECC RAMs configured and no Smepmp knob;
636	+   the spec conditions key on mmsc_cfg bits the RTL itself drives, and
637	+   the probe's checked read is the arbiter. Class A on our side (gates
638	+   fixed), no spec/RTL disagreement asserted.
639	+5. **mideleg reads 0x1444 at reset -- QEMU model agreement REQUIRED
640	+   (class B, resolved).** With RVH the H-delegation bits (2/6/10/12) are
641	+   read-only-one. QEMU models this only when it instantiates the same
642	+   CPU (`andes-ax66` with `h=on`); with the old ax45mpv family-default
643	+   pairing the oracle false-diffed (`mideleg ref=0x0 got=0x1444`,
644	+   `vlenb ref=0x40 got=0x10`). Fixed driver-side: `{qemu_cpu}` follows
645	+   the engine's qemu-config driver globals, and the `--verify` oracle
646	+   plan carries `hw_engine_id` so it models the same hardware.
647	+6. **QEMU andes-ax66 lacked Smstateen -- class B (QEMU-model gap),
648	+   fixed.** A guest `csrr mstateen0` trapped forever on the fast leg
649	+   (probe: `epc=0x100040 tval=0x30c022f3`). The engine's qemu-config now
650	+   emits `smstateen=on` when RVH/Smstateen is configured (converter
651	+   `f62337b`).
652	+7. **mcache_ctl / mmisc_ctl / mecc_code reset divergence (class B,
653	+   named).** QEMU andes-ax66 resets 0x1800 / 0x48 / 0x0; the mk RTL
654	+   resets 0x5000000100001800 / 0x148 / 0x800000 (RTL-hardwired read-only
655	+   bits). Harmless by construction (write-mask: unwritten CSRs keep the
656	+   engine's own reset), but a stash-compare read-back fixture cannot
657	+   pass -- per-engine `policy_overrides.csv` reclassifies the three as
658	+   verify-only. `--verify` still compares them on written workloads.
659	+8. **d23 (chh_core) macro-naming collateral (class A, fixed).** The
660	+   registration exposed that the macro NAMING axis (plain vs `*_INT`) is
661	+   independent of the decoder FAMILY axis: d23's plain-named CODENSE knob
662	+   was invisible to the kv-only `*_INT` binding (describe-vs-deriver
663	+   parity FAIL). Every generation-varying knob now prefers `*_INT` when
664	+   defined, else the plain name. d23 itself remains UNREGISTERED (its
665	+   `sim_d23` binary is not built here).
