+# CSR registration report: ax66_makatau (config 5937b880)
+
+Registered 2026-07-12 against vsim commits `e23700c` (family-aware caps) +
+`d0a8328` (S/U trap-CSR transport), converter commit `f62337b`
+(smstateen emission). Contract: `tests/engines/README.md`. Method: the
+three-way audit (`.claude/skills/csr-transport-bringup/references/
+three-way-audit.md`) -- SPEC = AndeStar_V5_SPA_UM164_V1.7 (per-CSR IM
+Requirement + Table 13; NOTE: UM164 is the kv-era SPA revision -- see
+Discrepancies); CONFIG = the build `config.inc`; RTL = the build
+`mk_csr_decode.v` (`andes_ip/mk_core/ucore/dru/hdl/`) `existent_csr`
+equation. FIRST mk_core-family registration: the CSR decoder, the config
+macro generation (plain-integer names, no `*_INT` twins), and several
+existence terms all diverge from the kv_core engines.
+
+## Engine shape (from config.inc + RTL + probe)
+
+M+S+U (`NDS_NUM_PRIVILEGE_LEVELS=3`), RV64, VLEN 128 / ELEN 64, RVH=1
+(hypervisor), AIA=1, SSTC=1. Perf monitor with 4 counters (Sscofpmf is a
+hard-1 localparam -- the Andes PMNDS scheme is hard-0 and never exists on
+mk), PowerBrake, PMA (16 entries), 4 debug triggers (NO tcontrol -- the
+decoder comments it out), 64K I$/D$ (CCTL CSRs), mstateen0-3 (ride RVH),
+mseccfg + mecc_code (UNCONDITIONAL in the mk decoder), no ILM/DLM (0 KB),
+no DSP/CoDense/StackSafe/CLIC/Smrnmi/PPI/FIO. QEMU pairing:
+`-cpu andes-ax66,vlen=128` -- derived at run time from the engine's
+`--print-qemu-config` driver globals (never the ax45mpv family default;
+that model silently keeps vlen=512 and models no H).
+
+## The numbers
+
+- Spec inventory rows: 232 (all in `csr_manifest.csv`)
+- RTL-implemented inventory addresses: 199 (probe, reset hart)
+- Claimed (transported) set: 35 gated names via `--describe andes_csrs`
+  (138 addresses including the base block, PMP mirror and PMA ranges)
+- `--verify` strict-compares 119 fields on this engine (rt_c_hello)
+
+## Completeness, both directions (empirical)
+
+- **Over-claims: none.** The probe cross-check (`gen_manifest.py`
+  recomputes it on every regeneration) reports zero claimed-but-absent
+  CSRs. Found and fixed during this registration: `tcontrol` (0x7A5),
+  `uzobctl` (0x808), `sleepvalue` (0x811) were claimed by the kv-shaped
+  TRIGGER/UMODE gates while the mk RTL has no existent term for any of
+  them.
+- **Under-claims: none.** Found and fixed during this registration (all
+  probed PRESENT while unclaimed): mseccfg, mecc_code, mpft_ctl,
+  mcountinhibit, mhpmcounter3-6, mhpmevent3-6, mstateen0-3, and the S/U
+  trio satp/medeleg/mideleg (transport decision, option A below).
+- Cold-cache hybrid `--verify` PASS, both trigger modes (fresh baseline
+  capture on this binary; the full claimed set swept on the RTL):
+  - marker: `[andesim] 54 cycles` / `[state-diff] PASS: 119 fields match`
+    / `[verify] PASS: vsim drain matches the QEMU oracle`
+  - pc (`--pc-start 0x100098 --pc-end 0x10009c`): identical 54-cycle
+    window, same PASS lines.
+- Generated fixtures (registration check 7): `csr_survival_gen.S`
+  (5 write CSRs) and `csr_readback_gen.S` (21 read-back CSRs) both
+  `--verify` PASS on this engine.
+- Caps parity: `--describe == config_inc_to_andes_caps.py` on all four
+  built engines (the mirror carries the same family rules).
+
+## Three-way translation table (every gated CSR)
+
+| Gate | CSRs | SPEC (UM164) | mk RTL term (mk_csr_decode.v) | binding (V<engine>_config.h) |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| ALWAYS | mxstatus, mclk_ctl, mnvec, mdcause | Always / Required | unconditional | -- |
+| POWERBRAKE | mpft_ctl | mmsc_cfg.PFT | `PFT_SUPPORT==1` (localparam 1) | `_NDS_POWERBRAKE_SUPPORT` |
+| ECC | mecc_code | mmsc_cfg.ECC | **unconditional** | always on mk |
+| EPMP | mseccfg | Optional (Smepmp/Zkr) | **unconditional** | always on mk |
+| PMA | pmacfg0/2, pmaaddr0-15 | mmsc_cfg.PPMA | unconditional | `_NDS_PMA_ENTRIES=16 > 0` |
+| PERF_MONITOR | mcountinhibit, mhpmcounter3-6, mhpmevent3-6 | Always (Zihpm) | unconditional | `_NDS_PERFORMANCE_MONITOR` |
+| SMSTATEEN | mstateen0-3 | Smstateen | `SMSTATEEN_SUPPORT==1` = `RVH_SUPPORT` | `_NDS_RVH_SUPPORT` |
+| TRIGGER | tselect, tdata1, tdata2, mcontext | Trigger Module optional | unconditional | `_NDS_NUM_TRIGGER=4 > 0` |
+| TCONTROL | tcontrol | Trigger Module optional | **no existent term (commented out)** | never on mk |
+| CCTL | mcctlbeginaddr, mcctldata | (ISZ\|DSZ) & CCTLCSR | unconditional | I$/D$ 64K > 0 |
+| UMODE | menvcfg, mcounteren, ucctlbeginaddr | misa[20] | unconditional | `_NDS_NUM_PRIVILEGE_LEVELS>=2` |
+| SMODE | mslideleg, satp, medeleg, mideleg | misa[18] | unconditional | `_NDS_NUM_PRIVILEGE_LEVELS>=3` |
+| PMNDS* | mcounterinten, mcounterwen, mcountermask_m/s/u | mmsc_cfg.PMNDS | **hard-0** (`PMNDS_SUPPORT=0`, `SSCOFPMF_SUPPORT=1`) | never on mk |
+| UZOB | uzobctl | misa.V \| mmsc_cfg3.AMM | **no existent term** | never (any family) |
+| ESLEEP | sleepvalue | mmsc_cfg.ESLEEP | **no existent term** | never (any family) |
+| DSP | ucode | mmsc_cfg.EDSP | **no existent term** | never on mk |
+| ALT_FP | umisc_ctl | ALT_FP_FMT \| CST_CTL | **no existent term** | never on mk |
+| ZCMT | jvt | Zcmt | **no existent term** | never on mk |
+| CODENSE | uitb | mmsc_cfg.ECD | `ISA_ECD==1` (param 0 here) | `_NDS_CODENSE_SUPPORT=0` |
+| STACKSAFE | mhsp_ctl, msp_bound/base | mmsc_cfg.HSP\|HSPO | `HSP_SUPPORT==1` (param 0) | `_NDS_STACKSAFE_SUPPORT=0` |
+| ILM/DLM | milmb/mdlmb | micm/mdcm_cfg.xLMB | `micm/mdcm` (sizes 0) | `_NDS_ILM/DLM_SIZE_KB=0` |
+| SMRNMI/EXCSLVL/CLIC/PPI/FIO | (their blocks) | (their conditions) | terms present, knobs off | macros absent = off |
+
+## S/U trap CSRs: transported (option A)
+
+satp/medeleg/mideleg are implemented on this S-mode core, drained by the
+plugin since v1, and -- new with this registration (PM decision, option
+A) -- restored at resume + re-read at drain + `--verify`-compared, gated
+on SMODE (vsim `d0a8328`; driver compare keyed on the describe names).
+An in-ROI read now sees the program's values instead of reset zeros.
+Other S-mode CSRs (sstatus, sepc, ... -- `EXCL_MODE`) remain deferred to
+the S/U-envelope work.
+
+## Discrepancies (classified, with evidence)
+
+1. **uzobctl 0x808 -- suspected spec-vs-RTL divergence (class D,
+   ESCALATE).** UM164 existence: `misa.V==1 | mmsc_cfg3.AMM==1`; this
+   engine has misa.V=1 (RVV configured), so the spec says EXISTS. The
+   probe reports ABSENT, and NEITHER decoder generation (kv_csr_dec.v,
+   mk_csr_decode.v) carries an existent term for 0x808. Note UM164 is the
+   kv-era SPA revision; the AX6x-era SPA may have moved/dropped the CSR.
+   Disposition: transport follows the engine (gate UZOB, off) -- but this
+   must be confirmed against the AX66 SPA revision and escalated to the
+   spec/RTL owners.
+2. **sleepvalue 0x811 -- interpretation-unresolved (class D-lite).**
+   UM164 existence: `mmsc_cfg.ESLEEP==1`. Probe: CSR absent; live
+   mmsc_cfg drains 0x8070e83340092015 (the ESLEEP bit position needs the
+   AX66-era SPA to decode with confidence). No decoder generation
+   implements 0x811. Same disposition and escalation as uzobctl.
+3. **tcontrol 0x7A5 -- none (spec-legal).** "Trigger Module optional":
+   the mk decoder omitting it is legal. The over-claim was OUR
+   translation error (class A, fixed: gate TCONTROL, vsim `e23700c`).
+4. **mecc_code/mseccfg unconditional -- consistent with the live
+   mmsc_cfg.** Present with no ECC RAMs configured and no Smepmp knob;
+   the spec conditions key on mmsc_cfg bits the RTL itself drives, and
+   the probe's checked read is the arbiter. Class A on our side (gates
+   fixed), no spec/RTL disagreement asserted.
+5. **mideleg reads 0x1444 at reset -- QEMU model agreement REQUIRED
+   (class B, resolved).** With RVH the H-delegation bits (2/6/10/12) are
+   read-only-one. QEMU models this only when it instantiates the same
+   CPU (`andes-ax66` with `h=on`); with the old ax45mpv family-default
+   pairing the oracle false-diffed (`mideleg ref=0x0 got=0x1444`,
+   `vlenb ref=0x40 got=0x10`). Fixed driver-side: `{qemu_cpu}` follows
+   the engine's qemu-config driver globals, and the `--verify` oracle
+   plan carries `hw_engine_id` so it models the same hardware.
+6. **QEMU andes-ax66 lacked Smstateen -- class B (QEMU-model gap),
+   fixed.** A guest `csrr mstateen0` trapped forever on the fast leg
+   (probe: `epc=0x100040 tval=0x30c022f3`). The engine's qemu-config now
+   emits `smstateen=on` when RVH/Smstateen is configured (converter
+   `f62337b`).
+7. **mcache_ctl / mmisc_ctl / mecc_code reset divergence (class B,
+   named).** QEMU andes-ax66 resets 0x1800 / 0x48 / 0x0; the mk RTL
+   resets 0x5000000100001800 / 0x148 / 0x800000 (RTL-hardwired read-only
+   bits). Harmless by construction (write-mask: unwritten CSRs keep the
+   engine's own reset), but a stash-compare read-back fixture cannot
+   pass -- per-engine `policy_overrides.csv` reclassifies the three as
+   verify-only. `--verify` still compares them on written workloads.
+8. **d23 (chh_core) macro-naming collateral (class A, fixed).** The
+   registration exposed that the macro NAMING axis (plain vs `*_INT`) is
+   independent of the decoder FAMILY axis: d23's plain-named CODENSE knob
+   was invisible to the kv-only `*_INT` binding (describe-vs-deriver
+   parity FAIL). Every generation-varying knob now prefers `*_INT` when
+   defined, else the plain name. d23 itself remains UNREGISTERED (its
+   `sim_d23` binary is not built here).
+
+## Test-generation guidance
+
+- Write-survival (5): tdata2, mhpmevent3-6 -- masks in
+  `safe_write_policy.csv`.
+- Read-back (21): mxstatus, mclk_ctl, mcctlbeginaddr, mcctldata,
+  mcountinhibit, tselect, pmacfg0/2, mpft_ctl, mseccfg, mstateen0-3,
+  mslideleg, menvcfg, mcounteren, ucctlbeginaddr, satp, medeleg, mideleg.
+  NOT mcache_ctl/mmisc_ctl/mecc_code (see `policy_overrides.csv`).
+- Ordering constraints: mstatus.FS/VS before FP/V state (probe + resume
+  handle this); no mcounterwen ordering on this engine (PMNDS absent);
+  satp/medeleg/mideleg are plain reads under the trap-free, paging-off
+  ROI envelope. Generated fixtures must park the hart (spin) after the
+  EXIT marker -- the mk halt latency is ~14 instructions and a
+  side-effecting exit store inside that window kills the `--verify`
+  oracle (see `gen_fixtures.py` TAIL).
+- Run commands:
+  - `./andesim run --mode hybrid --trigger marker --engine
+    vsim:ax66_makatau --verify <elf>`
+  - `./andesim run --mode hybrid --trigger pc --pc-start <S> --pc-end <E>
+    --engine vsim:ax66_makatau --verify <elf>`
+  - regenerate + re-prove: `bash tests/engines/test_registration_fixtures.sh`
